<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>

<!--
	Let's Have a Cat! Continued, by akairo and Bernau31 - akairo.LetsHaveaCat - twelve cat
	breeds on 1.6, none of which has a single coat variation.

	Eleven of the twelve get coats here. The black cat does not, and that is deliberate: a
	tint multiplies the sprite, so it can only darken, and the black cat's texture already
	averages 29 out of 255. Every tint on it would land within a couple of shades of the
	original. A feature nobody can see is worse than no feature.

	The rest are sorted by how much room their texture leaves. The white cat is the best
	canvas in either mod and gets five coats; the dark tabbies get two, at a low chance.

	Palette, in 0-255 form:
		soot      (122,120,124)    charcoal  (150,148,152)    ash    (168,176,186)
		chocolate (148,110,80)     sable     (190,152,112)     honey  (220,186,124)
		rust      (198,130,92)     fawn      (214,186,150)     cream  (234,222,198)
-->

<Patch>

	<!-- White cat - the one texture light enough to take any colour. Ginger, blue, smoke,
	     cream and a warm buff, and still white one time in five. -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName = "akaNEKO_shironeko"]/alternateGraphics</xpath>
		<nomatch Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<success>Always</success>
			<xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName = "akaNEKO_shironeko"]</xpath>
			<value>
				<alternateGraphicChance>0.8</alternateGraphicChance>
				<alternateGraphics>
					<li><color>(198,130,92)</color></li>
					<li><color>(168,176,186)</color></li>
					<li><color>(122,120,124)</color></li>
					<li><color>(234,222,198)</color></li>
					<li><color>(214,186,150)</color></li>
				</alternateGraphics>
			</value>
		</nomatch>
	</Operation>

	<!-- Persian - the other light one. -->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/PawnKindDef[defName = "akaNEKO_Persian"]/alternateGraphics</xpath>
